message.content:
Please do a thorough code review of this web scraper application. Look specifically for:
1. Edge cases that could cause crashes or bad behavior
2. Memory/resource leaks
3. Features that simply won't work as intended
4. Security issues
5. Race conditions or async bugs
6. Input validation gaps
7. Error handling gaps
8. UI/UX bugs (things that render wrong, state not reset, etc.)

Here are the three files:

--- FILE 1: server.js ---
```js
import { readFileSync } from "fs";
import express from "express";
import axios from "axios";
import path from "path";
import { fileURLToPath } from "url";
import { scrapeUrl, crawl } from "./scraper.js";

try {
  const env = readFileSync(new URL(".env", import.meta.url), "utf8");
  for (const line of env.split("\n")) {
    const [k, ...v] = line.trim().split("=");
    if (k && !k.startsWith("#") && !process.env[k]) {
      process.env[k] = v.join("=");
    }
  }
} catch { }

const app = express();
const PORT = process.env.PORT || 3000;
app.use(express.json({ limit: "10mb" }));
app.use(express.static(path.join(__dirname, "public")));

app.post("/api/scrape", async (req, res) => {
  const { url, useApi = false } = req.body;
  if (!url || typeof url !== "string") {
    return res.status(400).json({ error: "url (string) is required" });
  }
  let parsed;
  try {
    parsed = new URL(url);
    if (!["http:", "https:"].includes(parsed.protocol)) throw new Error();
  } catch {
    return res.status(400).json({ error: "Invalid URL" });
  }
  try {
    const result = await scrapeUrl(url, useApi);
    res.json(result);
  } catch (err) {
    res.status(500).json({
      error: err.message,
      tip: err.message.includes("403") || err.message.includes("blocked") ? "Enable ScraperAPI" : undefined,
    });
  }
});

app.post("/api/crawl", async (req, res) => {
  const { url, pathFilter = ".*", maxPages = 5, useApi = false } = req.body;
  if (!url || typeof url !== "string") {
    return res.status(400).json({ error: "url (string) is required" });
  }
  let re;
  try { re = new RegExp(pathFilter, "i"); }
  catch { return res.status(400).json({ error: "Invalid pathFilter regex" }); }
  const cap = Math.min(Number(maxPages) || 5, 20);
  try {
    const results = await crawl(url, re, cap, useApi);
    res.json({ pages: results.length, results });
  } catch (err) {
    res.status(500).json({ error: err.message });
  }
});

app.get("/api/download", async (req, res) => {
  const { url, filename } = req.query;
  if (!url) return res.status(400).json({ error: "url query param required" });
  try {
    const p = new URL(url);
    if (!["http:", "https:"].includes(p.protocol)) throw new Error();
  } catch {
    return res.status(400).json({ error: "Invalid URL" });
  }
  try {
    const upstream = await axios.get(url, {
      responseType: "stream",
      headers: { "User-Agent": "Mozilla/5.0...", Referer: new URL(url).origin },
      timeout: 30_000,
      maxRedirects: 5,
    });
    const ct = upstream.headers["content-type"] || "application/octet-stream";
    const cl = upstream.headers["content-length"];
    const name = filename || decodeURIComponent(url.split("/").pop().split("?")[0]) || "download";
    res.setHeader("Content-Type", ct);
    res.setHeader("Content-Disposition", `attachment; filename="${encodeURIComponent(name)}"`);
    if (cl) res.setHeader("Content-Length", cl);
    upstream.data.pipe(res);
  } catch (err) {
    res.status(502).json({ error: `Could not fetch asset: ${err.message}` });
  }
});

app.listen(PORT, () => console.log(`Running at http://localhost:${PORT}`));
```

--- FILE 2: scraper.js ---
Key issues to look for in these functions:
- fetchDirect: no response size limit, axios streams entire body into memory
- fetchCss: fetches up to 10 stylesheets in parallel
- extractFonts AND extractCssBgImages BOTH fetch the same stylesheets independently (double fetching)
- parseFontFaces: regex `@font-face\s*\{([^}]+)\}` fails on nested braces or multiline with { inside
- extractFiles: walks DOM twice (two separate $("a[href]").each loops), file dedup only by URL so same file with different text appears once but may miss entries
- crawl: queue.includes(link.href) is O(n) linear scan on potentially large queue
- crawl: no timeout on the entire crawl operation - can run for minutes
- crawl: if scrapeUrl throws on page 1, results array gets { error, url } object - then openCrawlPage(i) tries to call renderResult() on an error object which will crash
- getExtension: uses URL constructor, so relative paths like "../fonts/file.woff" passed directly will fail
- dedupeBy: if key field is undefined/null on multiple items, they all collapse to one

Frontend issues:
- triggerDownload uses URL.createObjectURL but never revokes it (memory leak if called many times)  
  Wait - actually the code does call URL.revokeObjectURL immediately after click... but the click is async so the URL may be revoked before browser processes it
- openCrawlPage(i) accesses lastCrawlResult.results[i] - if result at index i has { error, url } shape, renderResult() will crash accessing data.meta, data.summary etc
- switchTabByName called with 'images' after every scrape resets active tab even if user had switched
- The crawl depth input and filter inputs are shown even when doing a single scrape (confusing UI)
- No way to cancel an in-progress scrape/crawl
- If user hits Enter in url-input during a crawl, doScrape fires but buttons are disabled... actually Enter listener doesn't check busy state
- setBusy only disables buttons but Enter key still triggers doScrape while crawl is running
- stat clicks call switchTabByName which switches tab but doesn't scroll to results if page is at top

Please give me a prioritized, specific list of real bugs. Reference exact function names. Categorize: Critical / Medium / Low.

